## Why this is the strongest-fit role in the pipeline

Forward Deployed Engineer is the literal job title for Nick's pivot thesis: an engineer who embeds inside a real business, works out how the work actually gets done, and ships the system that fixes it. It rewards the exact combination he leads with - senior engineering depth plus the operator/consulting/product head - rather than treating the second half as a nice-to-have. This is a cleaner fit than the prior Senior Agentic Software Engineer role (4424527044), which was the on-thesis identity match but a pure build role. FDE adds the customer-facing, decompose-and-deliver, drive-adoption dimension where Nick has the most differentiated proof (Macquarie stakeholder delivery, the LIMSOC national consulting engagement, AccessBuddy solo build).

## Key JD insights

- **Embedded delivery, not arm's-length consulting.** "We do not start with tools. We start with the business." Maps to Macquarie (requirements direct with business stakeholders, 50+ hrs/week removed) and the LSV/LIMSOC engagement (inside a national org, authored and presented the scaling strategy).
- **Full-stack production code required.** "Production-grade code across frontend/backend (Python, JavaScript, or similar)." resume-swe carries Golang/Java/Python/TypeScript-React + GCP/AWS. Honest stack note: Nick's primary depth is Go/Java/TS, with Python in the mix - no overclaim needed.
- **LLM/GenAI deployment experience.** "Building/deploying systems using LLMs or generative AI." Dead-on: ANZ Plus AI search APIs on Vertex AI/Gemini, Claude Code daily, AccessBuddy agents.
- **Manage multiple deployments, sequence, remove blockers, balance scope/speed/quality.** Scrum Master at Leidos (2->6 teams), Macquarie 4-engineer lead, the national operating-model design.
- **Composure under high-stakes conditions.** Real-time regulated finance + a mission-critical emergency-response platform are strong proof points.
- **5+ years engineering, customer-facing.** ~6.5 years senior/lead, plus repeated direct customer/stakeholder delivery.

## The automate-first answer (the JD's required hook)

Built into the cover letter as a dedicated paragraph. The concrete pick: **the back-office coordination that lives in one person's inbox and memory** - status chasing, re-keying between systems, manual credential and approval admin. The reasoning is FDE sequencing method, not a feature pitch: it is the highest-frequency, lowest-judgment work in the building, so it is the lowest-risk to hand to an agent and the easiest to measure in hours returned, and shipping that visible win in week one earns the adoption trust needed to go after the harder workflows. AccessBuddy is the lived receipt (it automated exactly this class of work), kept as a supplementary closing clause.

